{
  "body" : "CONTENT BRIEF\nCreate a monochrome portrait of {{subject}} in {{setting}}. Use {{composition}}. Preserve a clear, readable face or primary form, with the expression and silhouette suited to the subject. No required text.\n\nSTYLE DIRECTION\nRender as a stark grayscale digital portrait with softly modeled, realistic tonal forms; deep near-black shadow masses; and a dense, mechanical pixel-and-scanline glitch that breaks up the upper portion of the subject. Keep the glitches sharply rectilinear: tiny grid cells, repeated horizontal rules, vertical bars, and fragmented blocks, with a few fine hairline signal traces. Use a near-black ground as the dominant field, cool neutral gray midtones, and restrained pale highlights; keep saturation absent and contrast strong. Light the subject from the front-right with smooth, soft transitions across facial planes, while allowing one side and the lower frame to fall into near-black. Blend crisp digital interference against softly focused, lightly noisy portrait detail; retain imperfect breakup and fine grain, without adding decorative effects. Apply {{glitch_amount}} while preserving the portrait's legibility.\n\nDESIGN RULES\nPortrait orientation, 1024×1536. Make the subject large and close, occupying the central-to-right region according to {{composition}}; let dark negative space dominate the lower frame and image-left. Keep the face as the primary bright focal area, with glitch detail concentrated above it and layered over the subject rather than forming a separate panel. Preserve a clear value hierarchy—pale face, mid-gray transitions, near-black background—regardless of the chosen subject or setting.\n\nAVOID\nColor accents or warm toning; clean, uninterrupted digital surfaces; evenly distributed glitch across the whole frame; bright or detailed backgrounds; hard graphic outlines around the portrait; decorative typography or interface panels; glossy bloom or cinematic light beams.\n\nAdditional constraints: {{extra}}\n\nVariables: subject, setting, composition, glitch_amount, extra.",
